{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]A woman had ten [Fmaj7]sil[Bbmaj7]ver coins
And one of them was [Gm7]lost
[A7]She lit a lamp and swept the [Dm]house
She searched at [Gm7]a[C7]ny cost
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Re[Fmaj7]joice [Bbmaj7]with me, [Gm7]rejoice with [A7]me
[Dm]For I [C/E]have found the coin I [Fmaj7]lost
There [Gm7]is joy before the [A7]angels of [Dm]God
Over one who turns back home
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Gm7] | [Gm7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]And when she found it, she [Fmaj7]called [Bbmaj7]her friends
Her neighbors [Gm7]gathered round
[A7]Come, celebrate with me [Dm]tonight
The lost coin [Gm7]has [C]been found
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Re[Fmaj7]joice [Bbmaj7]with me, [Gm7]rejoice with [A7]me
For [Dm]I have found [C/E]the coin I [Fmaj7]lost
There is joy be[Gm7]fore the angels of [A7]God
Over one who [Dm]turns back home
{end_of_chorus}

